            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for to get the jobs done, then the Mandarin for to look after."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 大米",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "大米 — dàmǐ — \"uncooked rice; rice grain\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "我去买大米 wǒ qù mǎi dàmǐ — I'm going to buy rice."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 米 (mǐ) — six strokes: two short strokes slanting in toward the middle, a horizontal, a vertical through it, then from the crossing a stroke falling to the left and one falling to the right. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "大米 (dàmǐ) is built from 大 'big' and 米 (mǐ) 'grain', both inherited from Middle Chinese, daH and mejX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second as the seed of a cereal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for asking for what I want."
            }
          ]
        },
